# Griffin design log
#
# Dated decisions, measurements, investigations, rejected alternatives and
# retirements, moved out of griffin.yml and griffin.md so that those hold only
# current facts.  Chronological, oldest first.  Fit numbers (LC/FF/PT) live
# here and in the fitter's .fit outputs, nowhere else.

Rev 1 bring-up (undated) -- AT89S52 IO MCU abandoned
  The AT89S52's P2 port drives D0-D7 with weak internal pull-ups (~50 uA) and
  something on the board held the bus during IO MCU cycles: P2 read back 0x3C
  when nothing should drive D0-D7 (expected 0xFF); scope showed one device at
  ~5 V and another at ~4.5 V on D0, consistent with a ~1-2 kohm path to GND.
  Communication worked only when the board ran abnormally slowly under logic-
  analyzer interference with CLK.  Ruled out: ROM (nROM_SELECT high during
  the cycles, at TP14 and U2 pin 20), RAM (all nRAM_x_SEL deasserted), CF
  (removed), the 74HC373 audio latch (pulled), VIDEO (reflashed with an
  explicit D tristate), ENGINE (unpopulated), GLUE decode (selects mutually
  exclusive and gated by bus_cycle; GLUE D bus tristated unless a GLUE
  register read), and a 100-iteration NOP delay before DTACK.  Also: the
  keyboard/mouse clocks had been moved off the interrupt-capable P3.2/P3.3
  pins.  Decision: XR68C681 DUART on a bodged DIP carrier for serial and the
  100 Hz systick; PS/2 moved into GLUE.

Rev 1 bring-up (undated) -- GLUE bit-bang serial and GLUE_TIMER removed
  A 5-bit /8 auto-reload GLUE_TIMER armed a DTACK stall for deterministic
  bit timing and drove bit-bang UART TX/RX on DEBUG_OUT/DEBUG_IN
  (timer_putchar / debug_getchar_asm).  Video DMA stalls and jitters the CPU
  and broke the bit loop, so both were removed; serial is DUART-only and
  crt0 brings the DUART up early.  A per-bit PS/2 assist in GLUE was
  replaced by the whole-frame PS/2 engine for the same reason.

Rev 1 bring-up (undated) -- 7200 /RE bodge wires rang
  Unterminated bodge wires on the video FIFO /RE lines rang and doubled
  reads (image creep); 10 pF to GND at the FIFO pins was the stopgap.  Rev 2
  terminates every FIFO /RE and /W at the source instead.

2026-07-24 -- possible new hardware features
  PS/2 mouse port: does not fit GLUE (grouping failure, every fitter lever
  tried); proposed for ENGINE.  Generalized ENGINE: stream into VIDEO, AUDIO
  or COPY FIFOs from RAM/ROM/CF, stream out of a COPY FIFO to RAM, optional
  block on the FIFO HF flags.  (Mouse placement superseded 2026-07-28.)

2026-07-28 -- PORTS, the fourth CPLD
  Fit experiment in cpld/ports (ten ifdef wrapper configurations, since
  deleted; ladder sources in commit 16ad819; full numbers in
  pcbv2-ports-design.md).  Two PS/2 frame engines will not share one ATF1508:
  the pair alone needs 140 of 128 nodes, and Foldback_logic, xor_synthesis,
  Logic_Doubling and TQFP100 all fail identically -- a channel is ~50 FF but
  costs far more once the foldback expands.  So the keyboard stays in GLUE
  and the mouse gets its own CPLD.  Mouse + 2 joysticks + 2 paddles + the
  audio FIFO pop = 111/128 LC, 80 FF, 41/64 I/O, 311 PT, first pass.  The
  74HCT245 / 74HC590 joystick and paddle chips are retired: the DE-9s and
  paddle ramps cost 0 FF and 21 FF in the CPLD, and the two 74155 read
  strobes and the DUART OP4/OP5 dump/clear dance go away (PADDLE_CONTROL.DUMP
  replaces them).  A programmable audio divider is not worth a chip (~30 FF;
  PORTS + divider = 151 FF, rejected before placement); halving the VIDEO
  HSYNC tap costs one flip-flop and gives the 15.73 kS/s the design already
  assumed, so the audio pop moved from VIDEO into PORTS ("VIDEO generates
  ~R" became "PORTS generates ~R").  The Rev 3 "dedicated ATF1504 for audio at
  0xFC0000" idea is superseded by the same measurement; 0xFC0000 is PORTS.

2026-07-30 -- GLUE and PORTS pinouts frozen; ENGINE IRQ re-wired
  Rev-2 GLUE logic always fit (107/128 LC in the experiment, 109/128 LC,
  57 FF, 326 PT as built) but routing failed with the rev-1 hand-assigned
  pins kept.  The earlier claim that it "fails no matter what" was wrong:
  the fitter auto-escalates to Foldback_logic but leaves Xor_synthesis off,
  and with -strategy xor_synthesis = on it fits.  Dropping -strategy debug
  and adding Foldback_logic by hand change nothing on their own; debug +
  xor_synthesis has crashed the fitter, so GLUE drops -strategy debug.  The
  pinout was harvested from a -preassign ignore fit, re-verified under
  -preassign keep, and frozen in glue.v's //PIN block: 63/64 I/O + 3/4
  dedicated inputs.  PORTS as built under -preassign keep: 118/128 LC, 80 FF,
  40/64 I/O + 2/4 dedicated inputs, 364 PT (vs 111 LC free placement -- the
  cost of the frozen pinout); xor_synthesis measured head-to-head on PORTS
  made no difference (365 PT either way), so PORTS does not use it.  Four
  ATF1508s built and fitting: GLUE 109/128 LC 63/64 I/O 57 FF 326 PT; VIDEO
  126/128 LC 53/64 I/O 99 FF 355 PT; ENGINE 91/128 LC 49/64 I/O 48 FF
  244 PT; PORTS 118/128 LC 40/64 I/O 80 FF 364 PT.  ENGINE had the only
  real headroom; PORTS had 24 spare I/O but 10 spare cells.  ~ENGINE_IRQ
  had been stubbed to 0 in GLUE during Rev 1 bring-up (610b06d), which would
  have dropped the port from the frozen pinout; re-wired as a live level-3
  input (ENGINE pin 5 -> GLUE pin 68) before the freeze.  The "ENGINE
  self-decodes its own MMIO" idea was never built; ~ENGINE_SELECT stays a
  net (GLUE pin 39 -> ENGINE pin 84) and is committed by the freeze.

2026-08 -- super-engine video path adopted
  Rev 1's in-band-header VIDEO + page-streaming ENGINE retired in favour of
  ENGINE -> {PIXELS, VIDCMD} FIFOs -> PIXEL (+TIMING) -> COMPOSITOR -> DAC.
  ENGINE's AUDIO_FIFO_W descriptor strobe added as a DMA fill path for the
  audio FIFO.  The rev-1 84-byte-stride in-band-header framebuffer remains
  only as the CF image container (VIDEO_LINE_STRIDE_BYTES etc.).

2026-08-10 -- VIDCMD read-port shaping gate proposed
  A 74AC00 NAND scheme to shape /RE for a 1-word-per-clock VIDCMD cadence.
  Rejected 2026-08-18 (below).

2026-08-12 -- VGA R4G4B4 output stage design handoff
  ATF1508AS -> 2x 74AC541 -> weighted-resistor DAC -> DE-15.  Buffers are
  mandatory (ATF1508AS VOH specified only to -2 mA; the MSB sources ~8.6 mA
  -- direct drive gives code-dependent nonlinearity).  Ideal weights
  500/1k/2k/4k with a 105R shunt; chosen E12 implementation bit3 = 2x 1k
  parallel, bit2 = 1k, bit1 = 2x 1k series, bit0 = 3.9k (2.6% weight error =
  0.03 LSB; do not double up), shunt 100R.  FS ~= 0.693 V loaded, Zth ~=
  72.7R.  74AC541 Rout (~10-15R) folds into the series values; optionally
  trim bit3 toward 487R if measured FS matters.

2026-08-13 -- COMPOSITOR -> PIXEL SET path: value bus
  A dedicated 12-bit registered value bus (set_pix_value) alongside the
  valid/target/commit handshake, chosen over a capture-strobe + fetch-stall
  design that measured +21 LC on COMPOSITOR and made PIXEL-target SETs a
  permanent 2-slot special case.  PIXEL's twelve former VIDCMD_Q taps leave
  the shared FIFO Q bus.  COMPOSITOR becomes pin-closed (63/64 I/O + 3/4
  dedicated inputs), accepted because its interface is complete.
  Same day: PIXEL+TIMING combined measured ~153 LC against the 128-LC part
  (pixel_combined.v kept as the negative result), so TIMING is a separate
  ATF1504AS PLCC44.  Stream FIFO parts unified on 2x IDT7200 per stream: the
  IDT7202s (1024 deep) specified for AUDIO are hard to source; 256 pairs =
  16.3 ms with half-full at 128 (~8 ms runway, ~123 Hz IRQ) covers the
  measured display-list fill of 49..93 pairs; XI/XO cascade footprint if
  depth is ever needed.  TIMING's vsync -> GLUE level-6 IRQ decided (revised
  2026-08-26).

2026-08-16 -- power entry and reset supervision standardized
  USB-C replaced by a 5.5 x 2.1 mm barrel jack: a plain-Rd USB-C sink is
  entitled to only 500 mA without CC sensing or PD, and the rev-2 budget is
  ~1.3-1.7 A typ vs rev 1's measured 0.84 A (rev2-electrical-review.md
  section 8).  DS1233D-5 supervisor; the D variant has no pushbutton
  detect, so button release rides raw bounce -- accepted (worst case a
  botched boot cured by pressing again; plain DS1233-5 is the drop-in
  upgrade).  Rev-1 C3 on the reset net retired (fights the CPU's 124-clock
  RESET-instruction drive).  Case wants a round cutout instead of USB-C.

2026-08-18 -- VIDCMD FIFO read port resolved: registered /RE, 2 clocks/word
  The 74AC00 gate scheme dies structurally: a captured word must be valid
  from T - tSU = 32.7 ns through the capture edge, so /RE must fall by
  32.7 - tA = 17.7 ns and rise at or after T - tDV = 34.7 ns; a half-period
  /RE rises near T/2 and data dies tDV = 5 ns later, so the valid window
  [tPD + 15, T/2 + ~6] misses every capture edge by ~8-15 ns in every
  phasing, and manufacturing the needed ~87%-phase edge requires a ~15 ns
  delay element whose tolerance stack (74AC00 tPD 2-8 ns, or an RC into
  non-Schmitt inputs) exceeds the window.  Rejected without a breadboard;
  74AC00/74F00 purchase dropped.  Adopted registered-/RE margins: see the
  2026-09-03 entry.  Consequence: VIDCMD cadence is 2 slots per
  word, 1-px spans render 2 px wide; propagation done 2026-08-19.

2026-08-19 -- VIDCMD 2-clock cadence rework done, all layers
  compositor.v + testbench: registered /RE with park-on-Q banking; 102
  checks pass incl. PAIR_LOCAL/PAIR_PIX banked-pair tests; fits 112/128 LC,
  down 4 from the value-bus baseline; Q is X-poisoned after /RE rises so
  stale-Q use fails visibly.  Measured: sustained cadence 2 slots/word,
  banked-pair gap 1 slot, PIXEL-target SET cost 2 slots, commit leads its
  slot's RGB_OUT by 1 clock, pipeline 2 clocks.  vidcmd-spec.md addendum
  (fetch engine, pair law, value bus replaces the Q-tap conduit, TILE
  dropped); super-engine render.cpp implements the fetch engine equation
  for equation; the author sizes CUSHION fillers from a vidcmd_plan_line()
  fetch simulation.  Suite all-PASS with one expectation change (m3-cursor
  84->98: HOLD widens 1-px outline segments).  Cadence floor: 1-px spans
  need >= 4-px pitch; the ENGINE delivery ceiling (~1 word / 3.6 px clocks)
  binds first at realistic densities.

2026-08-21 -- AUDIO FIFO /RS found unpinned (still open; see griffin.yml issues)

2026-08-24 -- MASK record implemented; cmp_held_fg/bg renamed
  The `01` prefix (TILE, dropped) carries MASK: two words, sixteen pixels of
  per-pixel overlay, no inline colour; data word reloads out of the park at
  pixel 8 with a HOLD stretch on starvation; header is playback-class.
  Measured seams: RUN->mask 0, mask->mask 0 (gapless), mask->SET->mask 2;
  derived mask->SET,SET->mask 4 and RUN->SET,SET->mask 3.  cmp_held_fg/bg
  renamed cmp_color1/cmp_color0 (VIDCMD_SET_CMP_HELD_FG/BG ->
  VIDCMD_SET_CMP_COLOR1/COLOR0), numbering and wire encoding unchanged --
  target 0 still writes cmp_color1 and target 1 cmp_color0; swapping the
  numbers is a wire-contract change deliberately not bundled.  Propagated
  to render.cpp, descriptor.h, vidcmd_plan_line, vidcmd-spec.md; m6-console
  and m7-kiosk render pixel-exact.  PIXEL the same day: late-cutoff fix
  costs 4 LC / 1 FF and saves 15 PT (one flip-flop); the four-stage delay
  line alternative measured 126 LC and failed routing on both passes.
  PIXEL fit ladder: as-was 116 LC/75 FF/398 PT; + bit_pos capture-clock fix
  108/75/366; + 2bpp indexed 112/78/414; + half rate 116/80/460; + late
  cutoff 120/81/445.

2026-08-26 -- TIMING fan-out package; COMPOSITOR/PIXEL/TIMING pinouts frozen
  PADDLE_TICK (17), AUDIO_TICK (18), HBLANK (19), nVSYNC_IRQ (31) added on
  spare pins by a -preassign keep fit; none of the original 9 moved.  Ladder:
  31 LC (frozen) -> 31 (+power_reset) -> 36 (+4 outputs, +line-parity flop)
  -> 35 (ticks toggle every line; parity flop gone).  Final 35/64 LC, 15/32
  I/O.  Ticks are square waves because a one-clock pulse (39.7 ns) is
  narrower than a SYSCLK; PORTS counts falling edges only because a
  both-edges XOR detector doubles the product terms of every paddle-counter
  bit and PORTS fails routing (falling-edge fits at 122/128).  The Rev 2
  draft's HSYNC tap into PORTS (31.469 kHz with a /2 in PORTS) is retired;
  TIMING is the single time base.  nVSYNC_IRQ is a dedicated TIMING register
  instead of tee'ing VGA_VSYNC pre-buffer, so the connector polarity can
  change without moving the IRQ edge.  DUART OP4..OP7 routed to TIMING pins
  20/21/24/25 as a future mode/rate selector; GCLK2 pin 44 left free.
  timing_tb.v created (closed-form laws, 12 output relations, 10 negative-
  control mutations).  ENGINE's HBLANK source pinned to TIMING pin 19.
  Alternate-raster and programmable-audio-divider fits measured (+19 and
  +22 LC, all = 64/64 with ticks + CSYNC) and not adopted.

2026-08-29 -- griffin.yml scope narrowed; VIDEO region and direct bus deleted
  griffin.yml is the source for CPU interaction, bitfile creation and
  high-level schematic validation only; rationale and history move here.
  The rev-1 VIDEO peripheral entry is gone: TIMING, PIXEL and COMPOSITOR are
  busless peripheral entries and video_timing lives under TIMING (codegen
  now emits TIMING_H_*/V_* and *_CLOCK for busless chips).  Nothing lives
  at 0xE00000, so GLUE's video_region decode and nVIDEO_SELECT are deleted
  and GLUE pin 40 is released (the region now BERRs).  The audio FIFO is
  filled by ENGINE DMA only (AUDIO_FIFO_W): the CPU-mapped AUDIO FIFO
  register at 0xC00000 is gone, and with it the whole 0xC00000 direct-bus
  region -- GLUE's ~IO_RD_EN/~IO_WR_EN (pins 36/35 released) and the
  74HCT155 fan-out; the three "reserved" quadrants (including the ENGINE
  COPY-FIFO candidate at 0xCC0000) had no occupant.  apps/smurf primes the
  FIFO with a one-shot descriptor list instead of CPU writes.  GLUE refit
  to confirm the remaining pins did not move.

2026-08-29 -- audio HF interrupt dropped; /EF and /RS brought to PORTS
  With the audio FIFO filled only by vsync-armed display lists (the firmware
  console re-arms every frame too), a FIFO-paced refill interrupt has no
  consumer; the pop rate is locked to the pixel clock (262/263 pairs per
  frame), so software dead-reckons the level and polls HALF_FULL at vsync
  as the missed-frame detector.  PORTS loses the HF latch, its W1C ack and
  the level-2 wire-OR (~PORTS_IRQ is mouse-only).  Added: /EF synchronized
  into AUDIO_STATUS.EMPTY (play-to-end / DAC parked), and /RS driven from
  AUDIO_CONTROL.RESET with reset value 1, which both satisfies the 7200's
  reset-before-first-write requirement and gives a flush; this closes the
  "audio /RS unpinned" issue.  Not adopted (yet): IDT7201 (512 deep) for a
  whole-frame burst per vblank -- 263 + cushion <= 512 allows one burst with
  a 249-pair cushion or two bursts with ~380, versus the 7200's nine bursts
  spread through the frame; depends on the 7201 being sourceable.
  PORTS fit ladder for the change (ATF1508AS PLCC84, -preassign keep,
  production flags; before: 122/128 LC, 371 PT, blocks B/C/F at 39/40
  fan-in):
    0. 2-FF syncs on /HF and /EF, RESET readback, /RE gated by RESET:
       keep -> grouping fail x5; free -> 121 LC, block C 17/16, fail.
    A. minus RESET readback: grouping fail.
    B. minus the /RE gate as well: grouping fail.
    C. raw /HF and /EF into the read mux (no syncs), /RE gate kept, no
       readback: free -> 119 LC / 366 PT fits; keep with the fitter
       choosing the two new pins -> placement fail then grouping fail;
       keep with nFIFO_EF : 48 and nFIFO_RS : 52 given in the //PIN block
       -> 120/128 LC, 368 PT, pass 1, no frozen pin moved.  ADOPTED.
    D. rung C plus the 2-FF syncs back, explicit pins: grouping fail x5.
  Finding: on a near-full ATF1508 under -preassign keep the fitter will not
  choose pins for new ports; give them explicitly.  The raw flags are
  justified because nothing in PORTS acts on them (the HF edge detector
  that needed the synchronizer is gone) -- they are CPU-polled like the
  joystick switch inputs.

2026-08-30 -- HALF_FULL dropped; PORTS pin 34 released
  With RESET giving a deterministic flush-and-deposit prime and the vsync
  latch already detecting a missed frame, HALF_FULL's two remaining jobs
  were covered; what it offered beyond that (a hardware check on dead
  reckoning about a frame before EMPTY) did not justify a signal nothing
  acts on.  nFIFO_HF removed from PORTS, the 7200 /HF pins are unconnected,
  AUDIO_STATUS is EMPTY (bit 0) + ENABLE (bit 1).  smurf's audio_prime()
  is now RESET pulse + fixed deposit with no flag guard.

2026-08-30 -- ENGINE strobes locked, ENGINE/CF status into GLUE, spare headers
  Pre-schematic net decisions.  ENGINE nSIGNAL[6:0] became four named
  strobes on the frozen pins: nPIXELS_FIFO_W 10, nVIDCMD_FIFO_W 8,
  nAUDIO_FIFO_W 6, nSIGNAL_SPARE 9 (to a header); pins 40, 41, 46 released
  and nDTACK_BUS (81) deleted -- ENGINE never sampled it, GLUE owns DTACK
  for DESC/CTRL.  The wider mask was kept for a write-capable engine
  (DMA to memory, DMA to CF) that needs a different ENGINE, not more
  strobes; edma2-class designs do not fit at 128/128.
  ENGINE -> GLUE status wires added, since ENGINE reads see the open bus:
  ENGINE_ACTIVE (dma_en) pin 80 -> GLUE 35, ENGINE_WAITING (state ==
  HBLANK_WAIT) pin 4 -> GLUE 36, read back with the IRQ net as GLUE
  ENGINE_STATUS (0x19).
  CF sideband added: INTRQ -> GLUE 40 (pull-down), IORDY -> GLUE 2 (pull-up;
  dedicated input pin, keeps 63 as the last free GLUE I/O).  CF_PINS (0x1B)
  reads both; INTRQ is level 1 gated by CONFIG.CF_IRQ_EN; IORDY is 2-FF
  synchronized and gates the CF DTACK term, BERR timeout unchanged (a card
  holding IORDY past ws_cnt 15 BERRs).  The CF dtack threshold was NOT
  lowered: that is a datasheet-timing decision for later, now safe to make.
  Spare headers: ENGINE nSIGNAL_SPARE/GND/+5V near the FIFOs; PORTS pins
  34, 41 + GND (unused I/O under Pin_keep_mode, no pulls).  Rejected: a
  spare bus between CPLDs (the chips with room, PIXEL 105/128 and PORTS
  120/128 with ~20 free pins each, have nothing to say to each other; the
  ones that do, ENGINE/COMPOSITOR/PORTS, are at 93-96% LC and COMPOSITOR
  has no output-capable pin left), D[7:0] onto PIXEL (bus loading, and it
  bypasses VIDCMD SET), strobes to CF (PIO cycle >= 165 ns vs 143 ns
  deposits, and GLUE owns IOWR qualification).
  ENGINE fit ladder (ATF1508AS PLCC84, -preassign keep, production flags;
  before: 123 LC / 77 FF / 414 PT):
    A. 4 strobes, ENGINE_ACTIVE = dma_en and ENGINE_WAITING = (state ==
       HBLANK_WAIT) as combinational outputs on 80/4: placement fail then
       grouping fail x4, does not fit.
    B. same, both status outputs as registered copies (one CPUCLK late):
       120 LC / 76 FF / 408 PT, no warnings past pass 1.  ADOPTED; the
       copies decouple the pin cells from where dma_en and state live.
  GLUE: 111 -> 113/128 LC, 65 FF, 308 PT, pins frozen; no grouping warnings.
  PORTS unchanged at 120/128 (comment only).  Emulator models
  ENGINE_STATUS (walker armed/parked/irq) and CF_PINS (IORDY=1, INTRQ not
  modeled); super-engine suite all cases PASS.
  Found in passing: firmware/rom.cpp no longer builds at HEAD
  (VIDEO_PIXEL_BYTES_PER_LINE gone from griffin.yml since 08-14); not
  touched here.

2026-08-31 -- Reset topology: supervisor diode split; GLUE halt-blink indicator
  Question that drove it: with GLUE mirroring the shared ~RESET net onto
  ~HALT, the CPU's own RESET instruction (124 CPUCLK) came back at it as
  ~HALT.  M68000UM findings (manualslib copy of M68000UM, pp. 73-76):
  external reset asserted DURING a RESET instruction is ignored (hence the
  132-clock rule for external resets); HALT alone is a bus-cycle-level
  mechanism ("normal cycle terminate and halt, continue when HALT
  negated", buses tri-stated, arbitration continues) and the instruction
  runs no bus cycles, so the echo was almost certainly benign -- but only
  by inference, and the plain DS1233-5's pushbutton detect (unlike the
  no-detect D variant) could have stretched the 8.9 us pulse into a full
  350 ms CPU reset (min detect time unknown).  Chosen: remove the
  question by construction.
  Topology: user button on the DS1233-5 RST pin (detect + debounce +
  350 ms re-stretch); Schottky diode, anode on the system ~RESET net,
  cathode at RST, so supervisor/button lows reach the net (VOL + Vf
  ~= 0.5 V < 0.8 V VIL) but the CPU RESET-instruction pulse and
  debug-header lows never reach the supervisor; RST also runs to GLUE
  nSUPERVISOR_RESET (pin 63, GLUE's last free I/O), which is now the sole
  source of GLUE's ~HALT assertion.  RESET instruction therefore asserts
  neither ~HALT nor the pushbutton detect; both griffin.yml issues
  (unstated ~HALT contract, DS1233 pulse-detect uncertainty) closed.
  Firmware still never executes RESET (the pulse still resets GLUE and
  restores the ROM overlay under a running CPU).
  Halt indicator: GLUE senses nHALT (double bus fault self-halt or
  debug-header hold; the CPU cannot report either) and overrides
  DEBUG_OUT with blink_cnt[4] of a 5-bit vsync-edge divider (~1.9 Hz,
  free-running off the 60 Hz frame rate; no 23-FF SYSCLK divider needed).
  GLUE fit ladder (ATF1508AS PLCC84, -preassign keep, production flags;
  before: 113 LC / 65 FF / 308 PT):
    0. combinational DEBUG_OUT mux + 2-FF nHALT sync: "fail to route
       variable nAS in Block 4", grouping fail x4.
    A. + registered debug_led_r output copy: still grouping fail.
    B. rung A + single-FF nHALT sync: FITS, 113 LC / 72 FF / 335
 PT,
       no warnings, pins frozen incl. nSUPERVISOR_RESET 63.  ADOPTED.
  1-FF sync justified: feeds only the LED mux, no state machine; a
  metastable sample costs one wrong LED clock (cf. the PORTS raw /EF
  precedent, 2026-08-30).  LED lags one SYSCLK via debug_led_r.

2026-08-31 -- GLUE sheds DEBUG_IN and nDUART_RESET; pins 64 and 24 are bodge spares
  Bodge-reserve audit before capture: GLUE was pin-full, and its two
  weakest pins were rev-1 leftovers.  DEBUG_IN (64) was the bit-bang UART
  RX readback, documented unused since serial went DUART-only; port,
  decode and read-mux leg deleted (reads at 0xF00001 now float like any
  undecoded GLUE offset).  nDUART_RESET (24) was a totem-pole copy of
  nRESET; the XR68C681 datasheet confirms RESET is ACTIVE LOW (clears
  SRA/SRB/IMR/ISR/OPR/OPCR, IVR=0x0F, OP pins high -- the reset state the
  OP4-7/TIMING contract already assumes), and griffin.md's rev-2 DUART
  plan already said "~RESET from ~RESET net", so the DUART's RESET now
  sits directly on the system ~RESET net (supervisor stretch gives it a
  clean long assertion; edge is the net's 10k RC rise, same as the CPLD
  GCLRs).  Both pins released as unassigned bodge spares (pin keeper, no
  pulls), to be routed to pads only.
  Fit (ATF1508AS PLCC84, -preassign keep, production flags): fits, 0
  grouping warnings, frozen pins held.  113 -> 119/128 LC and 335 -> 342
  PT despite strictly less logic -- FFs unchanged at 72, so this is the
  fitter choosing a different foldback/cascade arrangement for the
  changed netlist, not real growth; recorded as-is.

2026-08-31 -- Experiment: GLUE with free pin assignment (capacity check)
  Question: is the frozen pinout costing GLUE logic capacity?  Same
  netlist and strategy flags, -preassign ignore instead of keep:
    keep   (production): 119 LC / 72 FF / 342 PT / 16 foldback, pass 1
    ignore (free pins):  119 LC / 72 FF / 341 PT / 16 foldback
  Identical to within 1 PT.  Finding: the pinout constrains WHICH designs
  fit (grouping/routing, cf. the nAS Block-4 route fail in the halt-blink
  ladder), not how much logic this design needs once it fits -- no
  capacity is being left on the table by -preassign keep.  Production
  keep fit re-run afterward; frozen pins verified unchanged.

2026-08-31 -- Audio output stage designed; samples become two's complement
  Closes the last pre-capture issue.  Rev-1 baseline (netlist): '373 ->
  4610X 10k R2R -> LM358A unity -> 1k + 10 nF (fc ~16 kHz) -> 100 uF ->
  1k load -> 2x 100R to both jack channels (mono), 47R + buzzer on the
  jack switch contact; LM358B floating.  Known defect (2026-08 electrical
  review, re-ratified): R2R full scale 5 V vs LM358 VOH ~3.5 V at a 5 V
  rail -- the top ~30% of codes clipped.
  Rev-2 per channel: 7200 Q -> CD4049 inverter on Q7 -> R2R -> 10k to GND
  (the ladder's own 10k Thevenin is the divider top: exact 2:1, one part)
  -> 3.3 nF (single pole ~9.7 kHz at the 5k source, ahead of the buffer)
  -> LM358 half unity -> 4.7k class-A pull-down -> 100 uF -> 1k return ->
  100R -> jack.  2.5 Vpp max, +1 V below the VOH ceiling.  Buzzer kept on
  L via the switch contact.  Rejected: 2-pole Sallen-Key (needs a second
  dual now that both LM358 halves are channels), rail-to-rail op-amp with
  no divider (5 Vpp is over line level anyway), true bipolar analog
  (pointless behind the AC coupling).
  Sample format: TWO'S COMPLEMENT, 0x00 = silence.  ENGINE never touches
  data (deposit architecture), so the flip is 2 gates of a CD4049 between
  each FIFO Q7 and its ladder MSB.  MUST be CMOS-output: the bin's TTL
  7404N/74S04 VOH ~3.5 V would shrink the MSB weight ~25% at the zero
  crossing against the 7200's rail-level outputs.  4049 tPD ~50 ns skews
  only the MSB per transition; filtered by the 9.7 kHz pole.  Rejected: a
  software XOR 0x8080 per fill (about 1% CPU at full rate, and every
  mixer pays it forever).  Propagated: emulator DACs model the inverters
  (^0x80, idle 0x80), smurf audio_render mixes signed with +-120 clamp,
  griffin.yml AUDIO + interfaces entry, griffin.md, checklist.
  BOM adds: 2x 4610X-R2R-103LF (procure -- only one on the rev-1 board),
  CD4049 (bin, x7), LM358 (salvage rev-1 U15 or buy).

2026-08-31 -- Volume pot + LM386 internal speaker; buzzer retired
  Chain tail change only, nothing upstream of the coupling cap moves.
  Dual-gang 10k audio-taper pot replaces the 1k DC return (element top to
  the 100 uF, bottom to GND, wiper -> 100R -> jack), worst-case source
  ~2.5k at mid-rotation.  Internal speaker replaces rev-1's LS1 magnetic
  buzzer: the jack's NC tip and ring switch contacts each feed 10k into a
  mono sum (47k to GND for the open-contact state) into an LM386 at
  default gain 20, 10R + 47 nF Zobel, 250 uF to an 8-ohm cone (~300 mW at
  5 V).  Plug insertion opens the contacts and mutes the speaker (the
  rev-1 topology generalized); the pot sits upstream of the sum so one
  knob governs jack and speaker.  Software mute remains
  AUDIO_CONTROL.ENABLE.  Rejected: a PORTS-register attenuator (games
  already own loudness in the signed mixer; MATINEE has no CPU cycles to
  scale a stream -- the physical knob covers exactly that case).
  Procure: LM386 (not in bin), dual 10kA pot + knob, small 8-ohm speaker.

2026-09-01 -- CPU pin disposition captured; ~IPL2:0 and ~VPA pulls added
  Schematic capture of the 68010: E and ~VMA no-connect (no 6800
  peripherals); pull-ups on ~RESET 10k / ~HALT 4.7k (the net pulls),
  ~BR and ~BGACK 10k (float during ENGINE ISP), ~AS/~UDS/~LDS/R-W 10k
  (float on every ENGINE DMA handover and in debug bus-master mode),
  and -- new to the schedule -- ~IPL2:0 and ~VPA 10k: GLUE drives them
  push-pull but they float during GLUE ISP / blank GLUE, and floating
  IPL reads level 7 (non-maskable).  D/A/FC/~BG/~DTACK/~BERR plain
  nets; CLK via the oscillator's 33R series.

2026-09-01 -- Real RS-232 on both DUART channels; IP4/IP5 assigned DCD_B/RI_B
  The Aerie's Hayes needs real levels, and TTL headers were the one
  visible 2026-ism on the rear panel.  One MAX232 per channel (bin, x3)
  gives TXD/RXD + RTS/CTS exactly; ch B's DCD and RI ride a 75189 quad
  receiver (bin, x2) into the DUART's last two inputs, IP4/IP5 --
  poll-only, since 68681 change-of-state IRQs cover only IP0-IP3.
  Ch A console = DB-25F wired DCE (terminal straight-cables in; DSR+DCD
  strapped to the terminal's DTR).  Ch B modem = DB-25M wired DTE
  (straight to the modem, null modem to a peer -- matching the planned
  Aerie laptop hookup); DTR-DSR strap with the modem at &D0, hang-up by
  +++ATH, a GLUE bodge spare can drive DTR later.  TTL bench headers
  retained: TX fans out harmlessly; the four receiver outputs (RXD/CTS
  x2) pass through series isolation jumpers so header and port never
  fight.  MC1488 drivers rejected: they need +-12 V rails the 5 V-only
  supply doesn't have; the MAX232 charge pump is the whole reason to
  accept a 1987 part inside a declared reproduction.  No CPLD, firmware
  or emulator impact; DUART_IP_DCD_B/DUART_IP_RI_B masks generated for
  the Aerie software to poll.

2026-09-03 -- griffin.yml pruned of textbook, duplicated and rationale text
  Rule applied (now in CLAUDE.md): the YAML states only contracts a
  beginner-to-intermediate practitioner could not derive from the 68000
  bus, the parts' datasheets or the standard; each fact has one home;
  rationale, derivations, measurements, checklists and pulls live here.
  Deliberate exceptions kept in the YAML because they are the things that
  get gotten wrong: the DUART OPR complement and IP4/IP5 being poll-only.
  Material moved out of the YAML so it is not lost:
  - VIDCMD FIFO read port (COMPOSITOR): registered /RE, 2 pixel clocks per
    word, no shaping gate; all edges are GCLK rising edges, so no
    duty-cycle dependence.  Pinned parameters: IDT7200L15 tRC 25 min /
    tA 15 max / tRPW 15 min / tRR 10 min / tDV 5 min / tRHZ 15 max /
    tREF 15 max (REN_7200-7202_DST 20171127, 30 pF); ATF1508AS-10 GCLK
    tSU 7 / tH 0, clock-pin-to-output 8.0 ns max at 35 pF (DS20006682A
    Table 1-4); T = 39.72 ns.  Worst-case margins incl. ~2 ns flight and
    series termination: pulse +24.7 ns, recovery +29.7, cycle +54.4, data
    setup +7.7, hold +6.  /EF path: tCO 8.0 + tREF 15 + ~2 ns flight =
    25.0 ns vs T - tSU = 32.7 ns (+7.7 ns worst case).  COMPOSITOR ->
    PIXEL set_pix_value bus: twelve point-to-point traces, same clock,
    full-cycle setup, ordinary synchronous routing.
  - PIXELS FIFO read port: a byte is consumed every >= 8 pixel clocks
    (2bpp) or 16 (1bpp), so it needs no read-timing analysis beyond the
    VIDCMD one at 8x the period.
  - ENGINE HBLANK source is TIMING's registered h_cnt >= 640: not the
    HSYNC net (rises 116 clocks later), not ~H_ACTIVE (never toggles in
    vblank).  PADDLE_TICK and AUDIO_TICK are two nets so the audio rate
    can change in TIMING alone; event rate = toggle rate / 2.
  - ENGINE_WORDS_PER_BURST = 20: shorter than a scanline so one burst
    (~2.86 us at 2 CPUCLK/word) cannot fill an hblank (~6.35 us); long
    enough to amortize the ~10-cycle BR/BG/BGACK handshake.
  - PIXEL_PRELOAD_LEAD = 16: 2 first byte + 2 skip-discard + 7 alignment
    shifts = 11, rounded up.
  - Paddle counters: 255 ticks ~= 16.2 ms, one frame; the pot parallels
    the 1M pin-5/9 pull-up, hence per-unit software calibration.
  - Reset: DS1233-5 open-drain RST, internal 5k pull-up, trip 4.50-4.74
    V, 350 ms stretch, IOL 8 mA; asserted level on ~RESET through the
    Schottky VOL + Vf ~= 0.5 V, under the 0.8 V TTL VIL; the CPU's RESET
    instruction drives ~RESET for 124 clocks.  ~RESET 10k and ~HALT 4.7k
    pull-ups (2026-09-01 entry).  Bring-up gate: rail >= 4.85 V at the
    supervisor under full load, else DS1233-10 or trim the supply.
  - VGA DAC: FS ~= 0.693 V loaded, Zth ~= 72.7R, worst-case systematic
    error ~= 0.03 LSB (2026-08-12 entry).
  - CF_CMD_SET_8BIT constant deleted (rev-1 8-bit PIO; no users).
  - Audio-stage arithmetic (Thevenin divider, class-A bias, clipping
    headroom, LM386 gain floor and pads) and RS-232 cabling (DTE/DCE,
    MAX232 polarity, modem straps) moved to reminders.md.

2026-09-04 -- GLUE pinout re-frozen from a free fit; stray-pinout cause found
  Symptom: `make glue` at 14:34 produced a pinout matching neither the
  frozen //PIN: block nor a free fit.  Cause, reproduced exactly: the
  fitter had been handed an empty glue.pin (no //PIN: lines matched when
  run_fitter.sh grepped glue.v), and with -preassign keep and no
  assignments it places every pin freely while still logging
  "Preassign = KEEP" and "Preassign_file = " (blank -- that field is
  always blank; the pin file is picked up by name).  Not nondeterminism:
  the same edif fit with keep reproduced the frozen block pin for pin,
  and two -preassign ignore fits agreed with each other pin for pin.
  Per Brad, the //PIN: block is replaced by the free-fit pinout so the
  schematic labels are placed from a fitter-native assignment:
    ignore (free pins): 119 LC / 72 FF / 341 PT / 16 foldback, fits pass 2
    keep on the new block: 119 LC / 72 FF / 344 PT / 17 foldback, fits
       pass 5 (passes 1-4 placement/routing fail: nRESET blk 4; FC_2,
       A_lo_3, XXL_743 blk 6), pins held, run twice, identical.
    keep on the OLD block (same edif, for reference): 342 PT / 16
       foldback, fits pass 2, pins held -- the old block still fit.
  Changes vs the old block: nRESET moves off dedicated input 84 to I/O
  54 (no cost: glue.v uses nRESET synchronously, never as GCLR);
  nSUPERVISOR_RESET takes 84; dedicated inputs 3/4 used.  Spares are now
  pin 64 (I/O) and pin 2 (OE1/IN, input-only) instead of 24 and 64.
  griffin.md GLUE pin numbers (nENGINE_SELECT, nVSYNC, nENGINE_IRQ)
  replaced by signal names per the one-source-of-truth rule;
  schematic-checklist.md pin 63 -> 84 and spare list updated.
